Optimal Solution - Dijkstra-based solution using a min-heap to compute network delay time from a single source.
                   Use Dijkstra to find the shortest time from the source to all nodes, then take the maximum distance—if any node is unreachable, return -1.

class Solution {
    public int networkDelayTime(int[][] times, int n, int k) {
        // Adjacency list: node -> list of {neighbor, weight}
        Map<Integer, List<int[]>> adj = new HashMap<>();
        // Build the graph from edge list
        for (int[] edge : times) {
            int u = edge[0];
            int v = edge[1];
            int w = edge[2];
            adj.computeIfAbsent(u, x -> new ArrayList<>())
               .add(new int[]{v, w});
        }
        // Min-heap storing {currentDistance, node}
        PriorityQueue<int[]> pq =
                new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[0], b[0]));
        // Distance array to store shortest time to each node
        int[] result = new int[n + 1];
        Arrays.fill(result, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
        // Initialize source node
        result[k] = 0;
        pq.offer(new int[]{0, k});
        // Dijkstra's algorithm
        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
            int[] top = pq.poll();
            int d = top[0];
            int node = top[1];
            // Ignore outdated entries from the priority queue
            if (d > result[node]) continue;
            // Relax all outgoing edges from current node
            if (adj.containsKey(node)) {
                for (int[] nei : adj.get(node)) {
                    int adjNode = nei[0];
                    int dist = nei[1];
                    // If a shorter path is found, update and push to heap
                    if (d + dist < result[adjNode]) {
                        result[adjNode] = d + dist;
                        pq.offer(new int[]{d + dist, adjNode});
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // Find the maximum distance among all nodes
        int ans = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            ans = Math.max(ans, result[i]);
        }
        // If any node is unreachable, return -1
        return ans == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? -1 : ans;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(E log V).
Space Complexity :- O(E + V).
